  "query_preview": "..(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 340 PM EDT TUE SEP 29 2026\n\nThe extended period opens Thursday morning with a ~1020 mb surface\nhigh over the Southeast beneath a building upper-level ridge. Further\nupstream, an upper-level closed low (with central 500 mb heights\naround 570-576 dam) embedded within a broader southern-stream trough\nwill be centered over the Southern Rockies and Southwest. Recent LREF\nruns have trended noticeably more amplified with this pattern,\ndeepening the southwestern low while strengthening the ridge over the\nEastern US. This enhanced downstream ridge and strong southerly warm-\nair advection (WAA) across the Ohio Valley account for the warming\npre-frontal temperatures in recent guidance, supporting highs across\nEastern Kentucky in the mid to upper 80s on Thursday and low to mid\n80s on Friday.\n\nAn initial cold front will sink eastward toward the Commonwealth on\nFriday, drawing rich Gulf moisture up the Mississippi and Ohio\nValleys and bringing an increasing coverage of showers and a few\nembedded thunderstorms. As the southern-stream upper trough opens\nup and the surface boundary stalls near the Ohio River/Appalachians,\nshower and thunderstorm chances will linger across Eastern \nKentucky through Saturday. Temperatures will cool into the upper \n60s to mid 70s on Saturday under persistent cloud cover and \nintermittent rain.\n\nA secondary northern-stream trough will dig into the Great Lakes and\nOhio Valley Sunday morning, pushing a reinforcing cold front through\nthe region and steadily lowering rain chances from northwest to\nsoutheast through Sunday afternoon and evening (highs in the lower\n70s). However, as the main trough axis slowly sweeps across the\nAppalachians, isolated shower chances could remain along the KY-TN\nand KY-VA borders through Monday morning. Drier continental high\npressure takes full control by Monday afternoon, shutting off any\nremaining precipitation. While daytime temperatures remain pleasant\nin the upper 60s to low 70s Monday and Tuesday, clear skies and light\nwinds Monday night will allow cooler lows in the 40s to return to the\narea.",
